241</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10862506</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Ajith</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jose</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Janardhanan</surname><given-names>KK</given-names></name><article-title>Amelioration of cisplatin induced nephrotoxicity in mice by ethyl acetate extract of a polypore fungus, Phellinus rimosus</article-title><source>J Exp Clin Cancer Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>21</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>217</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12148580</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Mora Lde</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Antunes</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Francescato</surname><given-names>HD</given-names></name><name><surname>Bianchi Mde</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><article-title>The effecs of oral glutamine on cisplatin-induced nephrotoxicity in rats</article-title><source>Pharmacol Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>517</fpage><lpage>522</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12742005</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Husain</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Whitworth</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Trammell</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Rybak</surname><given-names>LP</given-names></name><name><surname>Somani</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><article-title>Protection by ebselen against cisplatin-induced nephrotoxicity: Antioxidant system</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biochem</source><year>1998</year><volume>178</volume><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>133</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9546591</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Ajith</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Usha</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nivitha</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><article-title>Ascorbic acid and &#x003b1;-tocopherol protect anticancer drug cisplatin induced nephrotoxicity in mice: a comparative study</article-title><source>Clin Chim Acta</source><year>2007</year><volume>375</volume><issue>1-2</issue><fpage>82</fpage><lpage>86</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16889761</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>CK</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>KK</given-names></name><name><surname>Lim</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>JHY</given-names></name><name><surname>Chung</surname><given-names>WY</given-names></name><article-title>Effects of the licorice extract against tumor growth and cisplatin-induced toxicity in a mouse xenograft model of colon cancer</article-title><source>Biol Pharm Bull</source><year>2007</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>2191</fpage><lpage>2195</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17978499</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Engel</surname><given-names>LW</given-names></name><name><surname>Straus</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><article-title>Development of therapeutics: opportunities within complementary, alternative medicine</article-title><source>Nat Rev Drug Discov</source><year>2002</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>237</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12120507</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Moriya</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Miwa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Orita</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><article-title>Antitumor effect of bacterial lipopolysaccharide (LPS) alone and in combination with lentinan on MH-134 tumors in C3H/He mice</article-title><source>Acta Med Okayama</source><year>1984</year><volume>38</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6702486</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Hamuro</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Takatsuki</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Suga</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kikuchi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><article-title>Synergistic antimetastatic effects of lentinan and interleukin 2 with pre- and post-operative treatments</article-title><source>Jpn J Cancer Res</source><year>1994</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>1288</fpage><lpage>1297</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7852191</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Matsuyama</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Mangindaan</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Yano</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><article-title>Protective effect of Schizophyllan and Scleroglucan against Streptococus sp. Infection in Yellow Tail (Seriola quinqueradiata)</article-title><source>Aquaculture</source><year>1992</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>203</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Matsuoka</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Yano</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Seo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Saito</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tomoda</surname><g